  "modelingNotes": [
    "The original curved OSM tower outline, orientation, 59-level tag and 210 m overall height are retained. No independently mapped building parts exist in this packet.",
    "The 2005 oblique skyline photograph and opposite distant view show the original straight-sided glazed slab, vertical ribs and shallow recessed top. Body eave 206 m, rooftop setbacks and terrace detailing are explicit visual inferences.",
    "Structural glass uses the approved light-blue palette instead of the historic dark tint. Grey vertical ribs and 29 double-floor bands preserve the facade rhythm within the map-scale budget; individual offices, roof equipment and signage are omitted.",
    "The model depicts the historic exterior seen in the selected references. It does not represent proposed renovations or certify current construction status."
  ],
